# ── gcloud credential stores — never commit, never track (OpsHero/GovCon item live-gcloud-credential-store-sits-repos-2026-08-10) ──────
# A live refresh token for the org-admin identity was found sitting at ~/repos on
# 2026-08-10, one directory above these repos, created by a task spec that set
# CLOUDSDK_CONFIG to a source tree. It had never been committed — but 8 of 9 repos
# would have tracked it if it had landed one level lower. Appended LAST so these
# win over any earlier negation in this file.
credentials.db
access_tokens.db
default_configs.db
legacy_credentials/
application_default_credentials.json
adc.json
*.boto
configurations/config_*
# ...and the same, at any depth: the pattern above contains a slash, so git
# anchors it to this directory only, and a config root dropped in a subdirectory
# would slip past it.
**/configurations/config_*
